From 7cd82b40a11a181d524cfb8a464a5f5c7ae5f860 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:11:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] turn_finalizer: the failed-tool-tail close row is
 the typed failed-turn boundary

A failed turn that ends on a tool row (e.g. session_persistence_failed) is closed by
_close_failed_tool_tail with a plain assistant row. That row closes the durable tail, so
conversation_loop's _close_durable_failed_turn no-ops and the turn never got the
FAILED_TURN_DISPLAY_KIND row with failure display_metadata Desktop needs to draw it as a
failed turn (error card).

Stamp display_kind=failed_turn on the close row and attach the same display_metadata
(_failed_turn_display_metadata) the boundary writer derives from the turn result. The
result's error/failure_reason stamping moves into _stamp_exit_failure so the row and the
result share one derivation. Test: a session_persistence_failed tool-tail turn (explainer
on and off) yields one failed-turn row whose metadata equals what the writer would compute
from the result, and the writer adds no duplicate.

Follow-up to PR #2066 review nit 1.
---
 agent/turn_finalizer.py                       | 58 +++++++++++++------
 ...st_turn_finalizer_interrupt_alternation.py | 42 ++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 82 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

